# [v2.5.9z104] H800 80 GB (Hopper, compute capability 9.0): the settings of nodes of this class only. The H800 cold start copies the
# export lines into that node's own $OPD_ROOT/control.env (env.sh sources it last); no other node reads this file. Every key is a
# setenv key (control_rules.KEY_RE), so `setenv` changes it later on that node alone (scripts/test_profiles.py).
# The arms' numerics as the B300 ran them (its setenv history: VENV=fa seq 121, FIXED_MICRO_BSZ=4 seq 21): flash-attn's venv with
# remove-padding, 4 sequences per micro-batch (the same loss partition as on the B300)
export VENV=fa
export FIXED_MICRO_BSZ=4
# Memory only, the math unchanged: the rollout's share of the card (the B300's 268 GB at 0.5; 0.4 of 80 GB = 32 GB for the weights
# and the KV cache), and the actor's gradient checkpointing on (the B300 ran GC=0; recomputation gives the same gradients)
export VLLM_UTIL=0.4
export GC=1
# Not here: the GPU count of the 8B arms. The queue's #gpus lines hold for every node, and an 80 GB node needs about twice the
# B300's; that waits for the queue on this node (Fable 10-28: health checks and one canary first).
